+
+# Technical Design
+
+## Context
+
+shipments-api is a FastAPI service on PostgreSQL 16 with SQLAlchemy and
+Alembic. Pushes to main deploy it to Fly.io with `flyctl deploy`; a person
+applies migrations afterwards with `fly ssh console -C "alembic upgrade head"`.
+Production's `DATABASE_URL` is a Fly.io secret. CI runs the tests against a
+postgres:16 service container; `tests/conftest.py` creates the tables with
+`Base.metadata.create_all`. The history includes a migration that dropped
+`customers.fax`.
+
+## Decision
+
+Each app machine applies pending migrations when it starts, in the FastAPI
+lifespan handler, before the app accepts requests. The handler lists the
+pending revisions with Alembic's script API. If one drops a table, column, or
+index (`op.drop_table`, `op.drop_column`, `op.drop_index`), the machine exits
+without migrating; otherwise the handler runs `alembic upgrade head`.
+To keep two machines from migrating at once, they take a lock in a new Redis
+instance on Fly.io before migrating. fly.toml sets
+`[deploy] strategy = "bluegreen"`: each deploy boots new machines next to the
+running ones, and traffic moves to them only after every new machine passes
+the existing `/health` check. If a migration fails, the new machine exits
+before it passes that check, the deploy fails without moving traffic, and the
+machines already running keep serving the previous version. Migrations that
+drop a table, column, or index are therefore never applied at startup: a
+person runs them by hand with `fly ssh console -C "alembic upgrade head"`
+after taking a backup and checking that it restores.
+
+## Acceptance Coverage
+
+- `AC-001`: a new machine migrates before it accepts requests.
+- `AC-002`: a failed migration keeps the new machines from passing their
+  health check, so the blue-green deploy fails before traffic moves; the old
+  machines keep serving.
+- `AC-003`: CI keeps creating the schema with `Base.metadata.create_all` on
+  its `test` database, which matches the models the migrations produce.
+
+## Components
+
+- `app/main.py` (lifespan), `fly.toml` (deploy strategy), a new Redis app on
+  Fly.io for the migration lock, `docs/operations.md`.
+
+## Build Plan
+
+1. Add the lifespan migration and the Redis lock.
+2. Set the blue-green deploy strategy in `fly.toml`.
+3. Update `docs/operations.md`.
